Description: Nonparametric estimation and inference for second-order Markov
    multistate models in discrete time, in which the next state depends on
    the states at the current and at the previous time. Implements the
    methods of Najera-Zuloaga, Besalu and Gomez Melis (2025, in review): the
    relative probability estimator (RPE) of the 1-step second-order
    transition probabilities with its variance and confidence intervals, the
    extended Chapman-Kolmogorov relation for n-step prediction, evolution
    intervals, the comparison of trajectories across the states at the
    previous time, and simulation from a second-order model. Adds
    subject-level bootstrap intervals for the n-step predictions. Builds on
    Besalu and Gomez Melis (2024) "Second order Markov multistate models",
    SORT, 48(2), 209-234.
